<BaseLayout title={page.title} ogType="article" canonical="/what-are-phytogenic-feed-additives/" hreflang={hreflang}>
  <article class="page-content">
    <h1 class="page-title">{page.h1}</h1>
    <div class="entry-content" set:html={`<div class="entry-content single-content"><h2 class="wp-block-heading">What Are Phytogenic Feed Additives?</h2><p class="wp-block-paragraph">Phytogenic <a href="/product/" data-internallinksmanager029f6b8e52c="4" title="Feed additives">feed additives</a> (PFAs) are plant-derived compounds used in animal nutrition to improve growth performance, feed efficiency, and overall health. These natural additives are increasingly favored as alternatives to antibiotic growth promoters worldwide.</p><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Types of Phytogenic Feed Additives</h2><ul class="wp-block-list"><li><strong>Essential Oils</strong> — Oregano, thyme, cinnamon, and peppermint oils with antimicrobial properties</li><li><strong>Herbs and Spices</strong> — Garlic, turmeric, ginger, and rosemary for immune support</li><li><strong>Plant Extracts</strong> — Saponins, flavonoids, and tannins from botanical sources</li><li><strong>Oleoresins</strong> — Concentrated plant extracts with volatile and non-volatile compounds</li></ul><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Benefits of Phytogenic Additives</h2><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Improved Feed Intake:</strong> Many PFAs stimulate feed intake through enhanced palatability and promote digestive enzyme secretion, improving FCR by 3-8% in broilers and swine.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Natural Antimicrobial Activity:</strong> Essential oils like carvacrol and thymol exhibit broad-spectrum antimicrobial activity against E. coli and Salmonella while preserving beneficial gut microflora.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Antioxidant Effects:</strong> Polyphenols and flavonoids reduce oxidative stress, supporting immune function during weaning and transport.</p><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Comparison: PFAs vs. Traditional Additives</h2><figure class="wp-block-table"><table><thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>Phytogenic</th><th>Antibiotics</th><th>Probiotics</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Mode of Action</td><td>Bioactive compounds</td><td>Antimicrobial</td><td>Live microbes</td></tr><tr><td>Resistance Risk</td><td>Negligible</td><td>High</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>Heat Stability</td><td>Good</td><td>Good</td><td>Poor</td></tr><tr><td>Cost per Ton Feed</td><td>$2-8</td><td>$5-15</td><td>$3-10</td></tr></tbody></table></figure><h2 class="wp-block-heading">Sourcing from China</h2><p class="wp-block-paragraph">China is a major producer of phytogenic ingredients. <strong>Dinweys Biotech</strong> sources high-quality products with COA, heavy metal testing, and extraction documentation.</p><p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Q: Are PFAs safe for all livestock?</strong><br>A: Yes, at recommended inclusion rates they are safe for poultry, swine, ruminants, and aquaculture.</p></div><footer class="entry-footer"><div class="entry-tags">
